      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working on some embedded c++ code for an automotive control unit and i've run into a problem. the system has a fixed amount of ram and after running for about 4-5 hours, it just hits an OOM error and crashes. i don't see any obvious malloc/new calls that aren't paired with a free/delete, but the heap usage just keeps climbing steadily. \n\ncan u give me a systematic way to track down where this leak might be coming from? i cant really run heavy profiling tools on the hardware itself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
